**What changed:**
1. **Selection-aware coding:** `cleanSurvey` now calls `targetRows_()` before `autoCodeThemes()`. If you have a data-row selection on the active sheet, only those rows are coded. A header-only or off-sheet selection falls back to rows 2..n.
2. **protectThemes flag:** When `true`, the protected range extends to the Themes column, for example `G2:Q123`. When `false` (the default), it stays `G2:P<n>`. The description and editor handling are unchanged.
3. **Helper:** `colToLetter_()` builds the column letters for the protected range.

**Things to know:**
- Turning `protectThemes` on changes the range, so the old `G2:P<n>` protection is not matched and removed. Delete it once under Data > Protected sheets and ranges, or it will sit alongside the new one.
- With `protectThemes = true`, volunteers can no longer edit Themes. The coder still writes there, because the script runs as the owner or an allowed editor.

Column Q is outside G:P, so the default clear never touched it. To honor your request for any layout, the cleanup now clears and writes each helper column individually and skips `outputCol` when `protectThemes` is true. If `outputCol` is inside G:P, its cells and formatting stay intact.

